speaker: Manav Mehra
---
bio:

An average person with above-average human intellect and strong curiosity to learn! I strongly relate to Peter Thiel when he says “Doing what we already know takes the world from 1 to n, adding more of something familiar. But every time we create something new, we go from 0 to 1.”

Born and brought up in India, I traveled across four continents to pursue a Master’s CS student at the University of Waterloo last year. I am deeply interested in Human-Computer Interaction and Robotics. On a side note, I have a crazy idea something that I call as “Transferring sixth sense over the internet” and would love to discuss about it!

I consider myself good at pool and I love listening to Daft Punk! If you’ve got an interesting idea to discuss lets connect @linked.com/in/manavmehra96
---
title: Growing Plants without Soil using Python!
---
abstract:
When most of us think of agriculture, we don’t think of it as a cutting-edge playground for AI, robotics, and data science development in Python.

This talk focuses on using Neural Networks and IoT with Python for implementing a smart and intelligent hydroponics (soil-less farming) system.
